#
# Packages allowed to have a build script (`custom-build` target), checked by `cargo xtask
# check-build-scripts` over the whole dependency graph (ADR-0023 decision 1, NFR-SEC-10). One crate name per
# line. Add a name only after reading its build.rs: no network access, no binary download, writes only
# under OUT_DIR. Downloader build scripts are banned (C-5).
#
# Reviewed at M0 (WP-S0.01): all of these run `rustc --version` or a probe compile to set cfg flags, and at
# most write a generated module to OUT_DIR.
#
# Added at M0 (WP-S0.02, xtask dependencies sha2 0.10 and spdx): generic-array 0.14.7 runs `rustc --version`
# through version_check and sets one cfg; libc 0.2.191 (via cpufeatures) runs `rustc --version`, and only on
# FreeBSD or Emscripten targets `freebsd-version` or `emcc --version`, then sets cfg flags. Neither writes files
# or uses the network.
anyhow
camino
generic-array
proc-macro2
quote
serde
serde_core
serde_json
thiserror
zmij
#
# Reviewed at WP-S1.01 (ew-units, ew-ids and their dev-dependencies). None opens a network connection or
# downloads anything.
getrandom # 0.4.3: emits a memory-sanitizer cfg flag only
libc # runs `rustc --version` (and `freebsd-version` / `emcc -dumpversion` on those targets); cfg flags only
num-traits # autocfg probe compile for one cfg flag (proptest, dev-only)
rustversion # runs `rustc --version`, writes version.expr to OUT_DIR
wasm-bindgen # wasm targets only in practice: version cfg via a vendored rustversion, link args for emscripten
wasm-bindgen-shared # hashes two of its own source files into an env var; runs `git rev-parse HEAD` (local)
